The logical date `ds` is injected into `extract` (which file to read) and `load` (which date to record in the watermark), so a rerun of a past day processes that day. Return values travel between tasks as XCom. The load is an upsert keyed on `order_id` (`INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE` in PostgreSQL), so repeating it, retrying it or backfilling over an existing range leaves the table in the same state. The helper functions stand for the verified model functions.

